Edits of the camera aperture offset and of a user screen window, see test_2819 and #2819

A sphere is rendered through a camera without a host framing. The horizontal and vertical aperture offsets and the
primvars:arnold:screen_window_min/max of the camera are edited: the offset moves the screen window and resets when it
goes back to 0, a user screen window is kept when the offset changes, and removing it restores the default window.
Each image is checked against the display window the screen window is equivalent to.
The scenario only runs with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last one is compared against the
reference image.

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
